# P13 batch 8
msgctxt "book 0572:07C7"
msgid "Honor Lost ~by Meltzars the Troll ~~ The state of my people leaves me distraught.  Even the name Troll is an insult humans hurl at each other, while in my time the name Troll was noble and respected.  What factors led my people down this path of twisted barbarisim I will endeavour to discover.  Since I was laid low by the sleeping disease contracted in my studies of the arcane,  there were no efforts to revive me, and now I see why. All trolls with any mystic skills are gone!~Indeed it seems that only the ignorant buffoons remain, and are breeding our society into mindless brutes.  After I awakened,  I was shocked to see Trolls dressed in no more than rags, and even more suprised at the garbled, vile insults they hurled at me.  After they drove me from their shelter (imagine Trolls living in caves like beasts) I encountered a group of our old allies, the Humans.  Upon sighting me, they drew weapons and charged!  My suprise was equalled by theirs when I turned and ran, believing these to be bandits or raiders.  It seems that a Troll who thinks of self preservation is alien to them.~My own clothes are torn and tattered, and it shames me to wear them, but it seems Trolls no longer harvest the silk of the kith.  If only I had learned to use the loom in my youth I would spin my own cloth.  I also hunger for fine wine and breads, but it seems my fellows have resorted to stealing toraxes from humans and eating them raw.  One of the Trolls I currently reside with brought in a Human child, and was going to eat her!  I would stand for no more, and blasted the Troll with a spell of light.  The others huddled away from me and stared with fear and hatred.~I will carry the injured child back to the gates of the human city. When the guards see my act of goodwill, they will hear me out, and perhaps I will find allies among them. "
msgstr "失去的榮耀~巨魔梅爾札斯著~~我族人的處境讓我心煩意亂。如今連「巨魔」這個名字，都成了人類互相辱罵的字眼，而在我那個時代，巨魔之名是高貴而受人尊敬的。是什麼原因讓我的族人走上這條扭曲野蠻的道路，我將努力查明。自從我在研究奧祕時染上昏睡病而倒下，就沒有人設法喚醒我，如今我明白原因了：所有具備神祕技藝的巨魔都已不在了！~看來的確只剩下無知的蠢材，正把我們的社會繁衍成一群沒有頭腦的野獸。我醒來之後，震驚地看到巨魔們只穿著破布，更驚訝於他們對我罵出那些含糊不清的下流話。他們把我趕出棲身之所後（想像一下，巨魔竟然像野獸一樣住在洞穴裡），我碰上了一群我們從前的盟友——人類。他們一看到我，就拔出武器衝了過來！我以為他們是強盜或劫匪，轉身就跑，而他們的驚訝不亞於我。看來一個懂得自保的巨魔，對他們來說相當陌生。~我自己的衣服也破破爛爛，穿在身上讓我羞愧，但看來巨魔已經不再採集奇斯怪蛛的絲了。要是我年輕時學過用織布機，就能自己紡布了。我也渴望美酒與麵包，但看來我的同胞已經淪落到偷人類的托拉克斯獸生吃。和我同住的一隻巨魔帶回了一個人類小孩，還打算吃掉她！我再也忍無可忍，用光明法術轟了那隻巨魔。其他巨魔縮到一旁，用恐懼與憎恨的眼神盯著我。~我要把受傷的孩子送回人類城市的大門。衛兵看到我的善舉，就會聽我說話，也許我能在他們之中找到盟友。"

# P13 batch 8
msgctxt "book 0572:10D5"
msgid "Expedition Journal, Book II~Day Seventeen... It's been about four days since Salem received the fatal blow, and some strange events have happened. Three children entered the camp before midnight, claiming to be childhood friends of his.  When she saw them, Iane let out a fearsome scream and collapsed, and the little strangers made a hasty retreat into the night. How could children be childhood friends of a man in his late thirties?~Day Eighteen... This morning around breakfast, Iane explained that the childhood companions were only illusions that Salem used to create to entertain himself, and if the illusions still existed, then Salem must still be alive.  We will seek advice when we return to Tenebrae.~Day Nineteen... After a rugged day of travel yesterday, we all expected a much needed and well deserved rest in Tenebrae, but it was not to be.  As soon as the door to our leased cabin was opened, those three children were lurking about inside. Still they pleaded for us to rescue Salem, and we had decided to let them stay with us and investigate their claims in the morning. The fact that they knew our destination before we did unnerves me to no end. There was no sleep to be had with the mournful gaze of the oldest child (who calls himself Collin) watching me all night.~Day Twenty... Today we went on a wild chase with the fire brigade as they attempted to douse several fires that started simultaneously around Tenebrae when a shower of flaming stones rained from the sky. Ianes skirts caught fire, and she raised quite a stir when she lept into the Tempest's fountain to douse them, and discovered it was stocked with snapping eels!~Day Twenty-One... We have spent the day on the road, following the directions of Collin. He has offered no information about Salem's condition other than he needs help.  After what I saw happen to him, there is no way he could be alive. What kind of help does a dead person need?  I guess we will find out tomorrow.~Day Twenty-Two... The black shadow of the keep still falls over us as the sun rises on the other side.  The silence and cold here is not natural, and Warwick is convinced we are being watched from the twisted spires. I am going to carry my speaking stone into the place, and it will recognize Salem without error. "
msgstr "探險日誌，第二冊~第十七天……薩勒姆受到致命一擊已經大約四天了，發生了一些怪事。午夜前，三個孩子走進營地，自稱是他兒時的朋友。艾安一看到他們，就發出一聲可怕的尖叫昏倒了，那幾個小陌生人便匆匆退入夜色中。孩子怎麼可能是一個將近四十歲男人的兒時朋友？~第十八天……今天早餐時，艾安解釋說，那些兒時玩伴不過是薩勒姆以前為了自娛而創造的幻象，而如果幻象還存在，那薩勒姆一定還活著。回到泰尼伯瑞後，我們會去請教別人。~第十九天……昨天經過一整天艱苦的旅程，我們都期待在泰尼伯瑞好好休息一番，這也是我們應得的，但事與願違。我們租的小屋門一打開，那三個孩子就在裡面徘徊。他們仍然懇求我們去救薩勒姆，我們決定讓他們跟我們待在一起，早上再調查他們的說法。他們比我們還早知道我們的目的地，這讓我極為不安。最大的那個孩子（他自稱柯林）用哀傷的眼神盯了我一整夜，讓我完全睡不著。~第二十天……今天天空降下一陣燃燒的石雨，泰尼伯瑞各處同時起火，我們跟著救火隊東奔西跑，幫忙撲滅火勢。艾安的裙子著了火，她跳進風暴使者的噴泉滅火，引起了好一陣騷動，結果才發現噴泉裡養滿了會咬人的鰻魚！~第二十一天……我們今天一整天都在趕路，照著柯林的指示走。除了說薩勒姆需要幫助之外，他對薩勒姆的狀況什麼也沒透露。從我親眼看到他遭遇的情形來看，他不可能還活著。死人會需要什麼樣的幫助？我想明天就會知道了。~第二十二天……太陽從另一邊升起，城堡的黑影仍然籠罩著我們。這裡的寂靜與寒冷很不自然，華威克確信有人正從那些扭曲的尖塔上監視我們。我要帶著我的傳話石進去，它一定能準確認出薩勒姆。"

# P13 batch 8
msgctxt "book 0572:17EE"
msgid " De-venoming the Kith ~By Ioria ~Removing the venom sacs from a kith should only be done to an animal between the ages of four to six days.  Sedate the kith by allowing it to inhale the vapors of boiling kalas leaves and mushroom spores. Do not breathe these vapors or intense headaches and dizzyness will occur. Once the animal is sedated, roll it over onto its back and locate the bony plate at the base of the mandible.~ Insert a wedge or pick into the seam at the base of this plate, and press firmly until the plate begins to slide. It will still be attached to the abdomen by several fiberous bands.  Lay the plate back over the abdomen and locate a pale membrane near the base of the mandible. Make an incision diagonally across the membrane and wedge it open. Inside there is a purple muscle. Slide this muscle towards the Kith's head, and underneath is a green or yellow gland with two tubes leading into the throat.~ Wrap the gland in a heavy cloth, and clamp off the larger of the tubes as close to the gland as possible. Cut the tube just behind the clamp, and firmly squeeze the gland until any venom in it has been forced down the remaining tube. Cut the second tube and lift out the empty gland.  Now stitch together the ends of the tubes, and fill the cavity with the boiled kalas leaves. Slide the muscle back in place, and stitch the membrane closed. Repeat the process at the base of the second mandible. When both glands have been removed, lay the plate back over the exposed area, and bind to the kiths's body with cord or bandages until it re-attaches.~Note: Some kith have no venom sac on the right side of the head. If the gland is not visible after opening the cavity, it may be one of these animals, but search the area throughly before closing the cavity. "
msgstr "為奇斯怪蛛去毒~尤莉亞著~摘除奇斯怪蛛的毒囊，只能在牠四到六天大時進行。讓奇斯怪蛛吸入煮沸的卡拉斯葉與蘑菇孢子的蒸氣，使其鎮靜。切勿吸入這些蒸氣，否則會引起劇烈頭痛與暈眩。動物鎮靜後，將牠翻成仰躺，找到下顎根部的骨板。~把楔子或尖鎬插進骨板根部的接縫，用力按壓，直到骨板開始滑動。骨板仍會由幾條纖維帶連在腹部上。把骨板翻回腹部上方，在下顎根部附近找到一片淡色薄膜。斜著切開薄膜，用楔子撐開。裡面有一塊紫色肌肉。把這塊肌肉往奇斯怪蛛的頭部推，底下就是一個綠色或黃色的腺體，有兩條管子通往喉嚨。~用厚布包住腺體，盡可能在靠近腺體處夾住較粗的那條管子。在夾子後方剪斷管子，用力擠壓腺體，直到裡面的毒液都從另一條管子擠出去。剪斷第二條管子，取出空的腺體。接著把兩條管子的斷端縫合，在空腔裡填入煮過的卡拉斯葉。把肌肉推回原位，縫合薄膜。在另一側下顎根部重複這個步驟。兩個腺體都摘除後，把骨板放回暴露的部位，用繩子或繃帶綁在奇斯怪蛛身上，直到它重新長好。~注意：有些奇斯怪蛛頭部右側沒有毒囊。如果打開空腔後看不到腺體，可能就是這種個體，但在縫合空腔前，務必徹底搜尋該部位。"

# P13 batch 8
msgctxt "book 0572:1955"
msgid " The Beauty of Rhian ~By Toran ~~~Her luminous candle guides my way in the darkness, warm and soft, my heart sings when bathed in her light. The gentle whisper of love calls out a name, Rhian. And my heart answers it.~Melody is her voice, whispering softly to my soul, a gentle chime of love. While I live, Rhian is my life. "
msgstr "芮安之美~托蘭著~~~她明亮的燭光在黑暗中為我引路，溫暖而柔和，沐浴在她的光芒中，我的心便歌唱。愛的輕柔低語呼喚著一個名字：芮安。而我的心回應了它。~她的聲音是一段旋律，在我靈魂深處輕聲低語，是愛的溫柔鐘聲。只要我活著，芮安就是我的生命。"

# P13 batch 8
msgctxt "book 0572:1CFE"
msgid " The Voices of Mary ~By Salem ~I wake in the night and the rooms are all dead, I follow a dream; she still echoes in my head, The new girl is twitching, asleep on the floor, I move through dark rooms, and pass through the door, Out in the chill, I follow the walk, The spirits aren't speaking, so there's no need to talk, The moon has arisen, to flower over the world, While tendrils of mist snake out, and slowly unfurl,~There's a sign by the sea that doesn't make sense, And out past the jetty wait sirens, horny and tense, Briefly, through windows in the pale glass waves, I see lost faces, ruined heroes in watery graves, I know what comes next, because I've read all my lines, I've been over my part, millions of times,~As the waters roll in and I'm swallowed by sea, I can hear Mary whisper, calling to me, 'Come on, baby,' from somewhere she cries, 'I want you to love me like spiders love flies'"
msgstr "瑪莉之聲~薩勒姆著~我在夜裡醒來，房間一片死寂，我追隨一場夢，她仍在我腦中迴響不已，新來的女孩在地板上睡著，身子微微抽動，我穿過黑暗的房間，走出門口，來到寒風中，我沿著小路前行，靈魂們不發一語，我也無須多言，月亮已經升起，在世界上空綻放，縷縷薄霧如蛇般蜿蜒伸展，緩緩舒張，~海邊有塊標誌，叫人看不明白，防波堤外，海妖們飢渴又焦躁地等待，透過蒼白玻璃般浪濤的窗，我短暫瞥見，迷失的臉孔、殞落的英雄，躺在水底的墓園，我知道接下來會怎樣，因為台詞我都讀過，我的角色，我已經演過千千萬萬次，~當海水湧來，我被大海吞沒，我聽見瑪莉低語，對我呼喊，「來吧，寶貝，」她不知在何處哭喊，「我要你愛我，就像蜘蛛愛著蒼蠅一般。」"

# P13 batch 8
msgctxt "book 0572:2640"
msgid " Eye of the Boulder, ~the Runes of the Myth Drainer ~My love, my life, my doom! I began my search for the Eye shortly after my nineteenth year, while still in training with the Necromancers. Had I known at that young age what would befall me upon the completion of my undertaking, I would have spent my days differently, seeking companionship over mystic power; warm love rather than cold stone. But my desire for the Eye was all consuming.~It is said to have been found at the heart of an otherworldly chunk of rock ,perhaps a part of some ancient tool or weapon, that fell from the sky during a time when godlike beings fought for dominance of this world and the worlds beyond. The Eye was later sundered into half a dozen finely chiseled runestones by the Leechlord, referred to in some texts as 'the Drainer of Myths'. The subsequent details concerning the runestones and their uses became the events of legend, as Tempests and heroes fought for possession of the pieces of the Eye.~ Though it took many years, it was I who finally managed to collect all the pieces. And with each part of the Eye that I added to my collection, my power grew, enabling me to recover successive pieces with greater ease. Obsessively, I laid the groundwork during those years of searching, preparing for the time when I could finally reintegrate the six disc-like pieces of the Eye.~ On the day of completion, once I had enacted the last of the rituals, my primary apprentice and I fitted the Eye directly into the freshly carved socket at the base of my skull, linking the mystic stone's energies with those of my own nervous system. Only then did I learn that the Eye's sorcerous operations were antithetical to my own. Immediately, its dire effects became apparent. My memory and other mental faculties grew weaker, the images I beheld lost resolution, and the sounds around me began to seem like bland reproductions. I left my hidden tower, staggering forward at a gruelling pace, one step at a time. And since then, the events of my days have seemed the tired tellings of a poor storyteller, and all I have wanted is release.~I am ashamed to have wasted so much time and so many of my resources upon such a disappointing thing. I sought nothing less than the Ultimate, but instead received only a pale reflection, a hint of what could have been. "
msgstr "巨石之眼，~神話汲取者的符文~我的愛、我的生命、我的劫數！我在十九歲那年過後不久，還在死靈法師門下受訓時，開始尋找那隻眼。要是我在那麼年輕時就知道，完成這項事業後會遭遇什麼，我會換一種方式度過我的日子：追求陪伴而非神祕力量，追求溫暖的愛而非冰冷的石頭。但我對那隻眼的渴望吞噬了一切。~據說它是在一塊異界岩石的核心中被發現的，那塊岩石也許是某種古代工具或武器的一部分，在神一般的存在爭奪這個世界與彼方諸界主宰權的年代，從天而降。那隻眼後來被吸血蛭領主——某些典籍稱之為「神話汲取者」——分割成六塊精雕細琢的符文石。此後關於這些符文石及其用途的種種，都成了傳說，因為風暴使者與英雄們為了爭奪那隻眼的碎片而相互征戰。~雖然花了許多年，但最終蒐集到所有碎片的，正是我。而每把一塊眼的碎片納入收藏，我的力量就增強一分，讓我更容易找回接下來的碎片。在那些年的尋覓中，我執迷地打好基礎，為終於能將那六塊圓盤狀的碎片重新合而為一的那一刻做準備。~完成之日，我舉行了最後一道儀式，我的首席學徒和我便把那隻眼直接嵌進我頭骨底部剛鑿好的凹槽，將這塊神祕石頭的能量與我自己的神經系統連結在一起。直到那時我才發現，那隻眼的巫術運作與我自身的完全相反。它可怕的效果立刻顯現：我的記憶與其他心智能力逐漸衰退，眼中所見的影像變得模糊，周遭的聲音也開始像是乏味的複製品。我離開了我隱密的高塔，以令人筋疲力盡的步伐，一步一步蹣跚前行。從那以後，我的日子就像一個拙劣說書人疲憊的講述，而我唯一想要的，就是解脫。~我為自己在這麼令人失望的東西上浪費了這麼多時間與資源而羞愧。我追求的是至高無上，得到的卻只是一道蒼白的倒影，一絲本可能實現之物的暗示。"

# P13 batch 8
msgctxt "book 0572:2949"
msgid "Captains report. ~ I recomend the new young guard Grommet for a commendation for bravery.  As a troll, larger than most, marched directly and purposefully toward our station, we prepared to destroy it from a safe distance with firegems. Before we attacked, Grommet saw that it carried in it's arms a little girl.  We hesitated in our attack, and he charged out and met the beast with his sword drawn.~In the ensuing  battle the troll was driven to it's knees, and as it begged for it's life, Grommet slew the creature. Some of Grommets blows flew a little awry, and the little girl was mortally injured by one of them. She was only a peasant  however, and of no import. Grommet will make a fine addition to the officers ranks. ~Captain Stovan "
msgstr "隊長報告~我推薦新進的年輕衛兵格羅梅特，表揚他的英勇。一隻比大多數巨魔都高大的巨魔，筆直而目標明確地朝我們的崗哨走來，我們準備從安全距離用火焰寶石消滅牠。在我們發動攻擊之前，格羅梅特發現牠懷裡抱著一個小女孩。我們的攻擊遲疑了一下，他便拔劍衝出去迎戰那頭野獸。~在接下來的戰鬥中，巨魔被打得跪倒在地，就在牠求饒時，格羅梅特殺了那個怪物。格羅梅特有幾劍揮得稍微偏了，其中一劍讓小女孩受了致命傷。不過她只是個農民，無足輕重。格羅梅特將會是軍官行列中的優秀人才。~斯托凡隊長"
